 After completing the problem, I found the use of Cauchy is very neat for this problem. </think> <answer> Applying Cauchy, we have
\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{1}{x + y} + \frac{1}{x + z} + \frac{1}{y + z}\right) (2(x + y + z)) \ge (1 + 1 + 1)^2 = 9.
