Thus $\frac{1}{x + y} + \frac{1}{x + z} + \frac{1}{y + z} \ge \frac{9}{2(x + y + z)} = \boxed{\frac{9}{2}}.$ On the other hand, if $x = y = z = \frac{1}{3},$ this bound is attainable, so the minimum value is $\frac{9}{2}.$ </answer>

